 boutiques","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires/Palermo_%26_Recoleta","hook":"High-end Argentine fashion and leather boutiques on cobblestone streets — the \"silk\" half of BA''s soul","si":"culture","blurb":"High-end Argentine fashion and leather boutiques on cobblestone streets — the \"silk\" half of BA''s soul","commission":"content-led; concierge personal-shopper","wells":["shop"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"La Boca / Caminito (daytime only)","tier":"essential","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/is-buenos-aires-safe-for-tourists/","hook":"The painted tin tenements, birthplace of tango and of Boca Juniors — a guided daytime visit only","si":"culture","blurb":"The painted tin tenements, birthplace of tango and of Boca Juniors — a guided daytime visit only","commission":"guided-tour affiliate / DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Tigre Delta day","tier":"essential","source":"https://luxurylatinamerica.com/blog/2023/03/13/day-trips-from-buenos-aires/","hook":"An hour north, the Paraná Delta''s maze of channels and stilt-houses","si":"culture","blurb":"An hour north, the Paraná Delta''s maze of channels and stilt-houses","commission":"activities affiliate / DMC day-tour","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — commission lane ''activities affiliate / dmc day-tour''","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Pampas estancia day — San Antonio de Areco (gaucho)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/best-buenos-aires-day-trips/","hook":"~1½ hrs out onto the grasslands to a working ranch: horseback, all-afternoon asado, folklore, and gaucho tradition","si":"culture","blurb":"~1½ hrs out onto the grasslands to a working ranch: horseback, all-afternoon asado, folklore, and gaucho tradition","commission":"DMC / MoR estancia booking","wells":["activities","eat","stay"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Argentine Open Polo (November, Palermo)","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.theaircharterjournal.com/air-charter-journal/argentine-polo-open-2025","hook":"The world''s most prestigious polo championship, at the \"Cathedral of Polo\" — grandstand and hospitality seats are a marquee November draw","si":"culture","blurb":"The world''s most prestigious polo championship, at the \"Cathedral of Polo\" — grandstand and hospitality seats are a marquee November draw","commission":"DMC / hospitality-package MoR","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","package"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Colonia del Sacramento day trip (Uruguay)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://luxurylatinamerica.com/blog/2023/03/13/day-trips-from-buenos-aires/","hook":"Ferry across the Río de la Plata to a UNESCO colonial town — the calm counterpoint to BA","si":"culture","blurb":"Ferry across the Río de la Plata to a UNESCO colonial town — the calm counterpoint to BA","commission":"ferry affiliate + DMC day-tour","wells":["activities","move"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to visit Buenos Aires for a honeymoon?","a":"The spring and fall shoulders — October–November and March–April — are the sweet spot, with mild 18–26 °C days and thinner crowds than the hot, humid summer. November is the standout: the jacarandas bloom lilac across Recoleta''s boulevards and the Argentine Open Polo fills Palermo, so treat November premium beds as a 3–6 month advance book.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"What are the must-see cultural sites in Buenos Aires?","a":"Start with Recoleta Cemetery — 6,400+ statues and crypts, including Evita Perón''s tomb, with free Spanish guided tours Tue–Sun — then Teatro Colón, one of the great opera houses of the world, and a daytime visit to La Boca''s Caminito, birthplace of tango. San Telmo''s Sunday feria on Calle Defensa rounds out the heritage circuit.","source":"buenosairesfreewalks.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"What is a puerta cerrada (closed-door) restaurant?","a":"They are secret chef''s-home supper clubs, a Porteño institution. Fogón Asado runs a Michelin-recommended 9-course asado tasting for ~35 guests with optional Argentine wine pairings, while Casa Saltshaker (est. 2005) does intimate shared-table five-course dinners with Malbec-vs-Patagonian-pinot flights — one of the city''s oldest such houses.","source":"theculturetrip.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Buenos Aires?","a":"Snatch-and-grab theft, not violence. BA''s characteristic street crime is motochorros (motorcycle thieves) and distraction scams, with roughly 90% of motochorro snatchings happening at traffic lights; keep your phone off café-table edges and use vetted radio-taxi or ride-apps. La Boca is daytime-and-Caminito only — arrive by taxi and leave before dark.","source":"secretsofbuenosaires.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"Do I need travel insurance for Argentina?","a":"Treat it as required and always buy it. Under Decree 366/2025, effective 2025-07-01, non-resident travelers were required to carry travel medical insurance covering emergency care, hospitalization, evacuation and repatriation, with airlines confirming at check-in. One December-2025 secondary source reported the rule may have been suspended or modified (unverified and conflicting), so verify current enforcement at booking.","source":"globalrescue.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Buenos Aires Travel Guide — Tango, Steak & Boutique Hotels | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-AR","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Buenos Aires","show de tango Buenos Aires","mejores parrillas Buenos Aires","puertas cerradas Buenos Aires","Cementerio de la Recoleta Evita","estancia San Antonio de Areco","escapada al Delta del Tigre","hoteles de lujo Buenos Aires","Abierto Argentino de Polo","mejor época para visitar Buenos Aires"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/argentina","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:24Z","source_updated":"2026-05-07T17:26:11+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07","long_tail":["things to do in Buenos Aires","best tango show Buenos Aires","closed-door restaurants Buenos Aires","Buenos Aires honeymoon","best time to visit Buenos Aires","Recoleta cemetery Evita","Tigre Delta day trip","San Antonio de Areco estancia","Buenos Aires luxury hotels","is Buenos Aires safe"]},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Buenos Aires + La Mansion","barrio":"Recoleta","tier":"ultra","earning":"FS Preferred Partner / Virtuoso — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"},{"name":"Alvear Palace Hotel","barrio":"Recoleta","tier":"ultra","earning":"Virtuoso / LHW — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"},{"name":"Palacio Duhau — Park Hyatt Buenos Aires","barrio":"Recoleta","tier":"ultra","earning":"Hyatt Prive / Virtuoso — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"},{"name":"Faena Hotel Buenos Aires","barrio":"Puerto Madero","tier":"ultra","earning":"Virtuoso / brand luxury — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Buenos Aires, Argentina, Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-34.6037,"lng":-58.3816},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["el-calafate-argentina","iguazu-falls-argentina","mendoza-argentina","peninsula-valdes-argentina","salta-argentina"]}'::jsonb, 15),
