amed beside it on the date shown. ⛔ A number with no entry here has NOT been verified and must not be presented as an emergency contact."}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Mar (calmest seas, clearest skies, 200ft+ viz; Dec24-Jan1 crowded/expensive spike)","shoulder":"Nov (~25-40% off Dec) and May (~20-30% off April); near-peak conditions","green":"May-Sep warmest water ~27-28C / calmest seas; summer humidity + hurricane risk Jun-Nov (peak Aug-Oct)","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"green-summer value story: warmest/calmest water + 20-40% off rooms, thinner crowds, pair with hurricane trip insurance","fire_date":"open peak-season campaign Aug-Sep for Dec-Mar; shoulder push Sep-Oct (Nov) and Feb-Mar (May); Carnival micro-campaign Nov-Dec for mid-Feb","event_peaks":["Cozumel Carnival 2026: main parades Feb 14/15/17 (Fat Tue), run Feb 11-18, pre-Carnival Jan 17-Feb 8; floats with pre-Lenten lunar calendar","cruise-ship day-crowds congest San Miguel + nearer reefs — push early boats / south-zone sites"],"booking_lead":"peak dive weeks book well ahead; Chinchorro multi-day + private crewed dive-yacht = book months ahead (limited weather windows / small vessels)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Palancar Reef (Gardens/Caves/Bricks/Horseshoe)","status":"future","bookable":"2-tank day-boat dive","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.torntackies.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","hook":"iconic coral pinnacles, archways, swim-throughs, 100-ft+ viz, accessible drift","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"iconic coral pinnacles, archways, swim-throughs, 100-ft+ viz, accessible drift","commission":"dive-op DMC + Viator affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["diveglobal"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"primary","liveaboard":"destination","ocean":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator","DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Santa Rosa Wall","status":"future","bookable":"advanced day-boat dive (expert-only)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.torntackies.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"starts ~15 m / 45 ft and drops into the deep; expert-level, with eagle rays, turtles, nurse sharks and giant morays","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"starts ~15 m / 45 ft and drops into the deep; expert-level, with eagle rays, turtles, nurse sharks and giant morays","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"dive-op DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["diveglobal"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"primary","liveaboard":"destination","ocean":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator","DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Columbia Deep","status":"future","bookable":"advanced day-boat dive","tier":"comfort","source":"https://cozumelscuba.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"dive-op DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — commission lane ''dive-op dmc''","si_all":["diveglobal"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"primary","liveaboard":"destination","ocean":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator","DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Banco Chinchorro atoll","status":"future","bookable":"multi-day/liveaboard-style from Xcalak/Mahahual","tier":"premier","source":"http://www.pelagiclife.org/chinchorro","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"Aggressor/liveaboard reseller = Commissioned Agent on application","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — si (unambiguous spend type)","si_all":["liveaboard"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"destination","liveaboard":"primary","ocean":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Palancar snorkel + El Cielo sandbar","status":"future","bookable":"catamaran/snorkel tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://cozumelscuba.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","hook":"reef snorkel and shallow turquoise sandbar, no-fly-free family option","si":"ocean","blurb":"reef snorkel and shallow turquoise sandbar, no-fly-free family option","commission":"Viator/GYG affiliate + DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal","ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","liveaboard":"destination","ocean":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cozumel?","a":"Decompression discipline, not crime — this is a repetitive multi-day dive island. Follow DAN''s no-fly windows strictly (12h single, 18h multi-day, 24h conservative), because Cozumel''s day-boat profiles stack dives fast; the island has multiple chambers, but a bad no-fly call is the classic mistake. Also plan for dengue (repellent), bottled water and hurricane season (Jun–Nov).","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is drift diving in Cozumel dangerous?","a":"No, when you take the drift briefing seriously — but it is not passive. Expect a near-constant ~1.5-knot current that does the swimming for you; do a controlled descent, stay with the group and dive master, deploy an SMB, and dive within your certification. Santa Rosa Wall is expert-only; Palancar Gardens suits most certified divers.","source":"cozumelscuba.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"What are the best dive sites in Cozumel, and can beginners dive them?","a":"Palancar Gardens is the everyone-friendly classic — coral pinnacles, archways and swim-throughs at 100-ft-plus visibility with mild current — while Santa Rosa Wall and Columbia Deep are advanced drifts. Beginners and newly certified divers do best at Palancar; Santa Rosa, dropping from ~15 m into the blue, is expert-only.","source":"torntackies.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"Can I do a liveaboard from Cozumel?","a":"Not from Cozumel itself — it is a day-boat island. True liveaboard-style multi-day diving goes to Banco Chinchorro, ~30–35 nm off Costa Maya, launched from Xcalak or Mahahual to the south, not Cozumel. The luxury alternative near Cozumel is a private crewed dive-yacht charter, since overnight liveaboards are effectively banned inside the national park.","source":"pelagiclife.org / islandlifemexico.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"liveaboard","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"Can non-divers snorkel Cozumel, and what''s the reef fee?","a":"Yes — the reef is superb for snorkelers, from Palancar shallows to the El Cielo starfish sandbar by catamaran. Everyone entering the marine park pays the reef bracelet, MX$220 (~US$13) per person per day as of Jan 2026; snorkel tours carry no no-fly restriction, making them a good last-day option before a flight.","source":"cozumelmio.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"Is Cozumel good for a honeymoon or a couples'' dive trip?","a":"Yes — it pairs world-class diving with real staffed villas. Luxury Cozumel and Villa Experience run oceanfront staffed homes (chef, concierge) from ~US$450/night, and there is no branded ultra flag on-island, so for hotel-brand luxury couples ferry to Mayakoba (Rosewood, Banyan Tree) ~an hour away.","source":"luxurycozumel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive Cozumel?","a":"December–March is peak, with the calmest seas, clearest skies and legendary 200-ft-plus visibility. November and May are the value sweet spots — near-peak conditions at ~25–40% (Nov) and ~20–30% (May) below Dec rates; May–September brings the warmest, calmest water (~27–28°C) but summer humidity and hurricane risk.","source":"sunsetcozumel.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cozumel Diving: Drift the Mesoamerican Reef","meta_description":"Cozumel is the Caribbean''s drift-diving crown - Palancar, Santa Rosa Wall and the Mesoamerican Reef, with chambers, no-fly rules and the Chinchorro liveaboard hook.","slug":"cozumel-mexico","primary_keyword":"Cozumel drift diving","long_tail":["Cozumel dive sites Palancar Santa Rosa","Cozumel marine park fee 2026","Banco Chinchorro liveaboard","Cozumel recompression chamber","Mesoamerican Barrier Reef diving"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["buceo en Cozumel","arrecife Palancar Santa Rosa","camara hiperbarica Cozumel","buceo de deriva Cozumel","Parque Nacional Arrecifes de Cozumel","Banco Chinchorro buceo","villa privada de lujo Cozumel"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-04","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"liveaboard","status":"future","note":"Cozumel = day-boat reef diving; liveaboard/multi-day runs to Banco Chinchorro launch from Xcalak/Mahahual, NOT Cozumel"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private Paradise Villa","location":"Cozumel (on-island)","what":"oceanfront exclusive-use villa, sleeps up to 24, 40+ staff incl. 7 rotating chefs + British-butler-trained butlers","why_ultra":"full-buyout fully-staffed private-resort — the on-island ultra expression","earning":"villa-agency/DMC commission on application (agent-of-record; no net-rate resale)","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a standalone; attach Virtuoso mainland stay for perks","mor_posture":"clean agent-side; red-flag any villa-inventory mark-up","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://privateparadisevilla.com/"},{"name":"Private crewed dive-yacht charter","location":"Cozumel / Riviera Maya (on-water)","what":"fully-crewed private yacht (captain+deckhand+dive master, chef/hostess on premium boats), 15+ sites + El Cielo, premium open bar","why_ultra":"ultra dive expression; only luxury ''liveaboard-style'' the park''s vessel-size rules allow (overnight liveaboards effectively banned in-park)","earning":"charter/DMC commission on application","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a direct; pair with Virtuoso stay","mor_posture":"agent-of-record on charter; no net-rate resale","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://dayyachtcharters.com/cozumel-yacht-charters-luxury-boat-rentals.html"},{"name":"Riviera Maya branded ultra (Rosewood/Banyan Tree Mayakoba, Chable Maroma, Maroma Belmond)","location":"Riviera Maya mainland (ferry + short transfer)","what":"Forbes/branded ultra-luxury resorts + villas; private pools, top spas, PGA course","why_ultra":"nearest true branded ultra flag — no ultra flag on Cozumel itself","earning":"Virtuoso preferred rate + commission (or via host-Virtuoso)","virtuoso_value_add":"upgrade, daily breakfast for two, early check-in/late check-out, ~US$100 credit, VIP welcome (Mayakoba flags)","mor_posture":"standard Virtuoso agent-of-record","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/en/mayakoba-riviera-maya"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Cozumel, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.423,"lng":-86.9223},"orbit":[{"id":"akumal-mexico","jewels